WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.272
Appendix B is the starting matrix
that seeds wave 1, and the rule is

2
00:00:04.272 --> 00:00:08.650
to classify each template by what it
actually issued, not by its name.

3
00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:10.825
A few facts decide most rows.

4
00:00:10.825 --> 00:00:16.223
Cloud PKI issues only to Intune devices,
and Intune doesn't manage servers,

5
00:00:16.223 --> 00:00:20.825
so every server certificate is
bridge or retain, never migrate.

6
00:00:20.825 --> 00:00:25.558
For example, the old guide moved Web
Server to Cloud PKI, but web servers

7
00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:31.025
aren't Intune devices, so it stays, renewed
through CyberArk Certificate Manager.

8
00:00:31.025 --> 00:00:36.450
Some templates even carry two verdicts,
migrating delivery while the issuer stays.

9
00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:40.270
Before any migrate row moves,
it has to pass four checks,

10
00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:42.987
which become wave 4's per-ring exit test.

11
00:00:42.987 --> 00:00:46.164
And every bridge row records
the event that ends it,

12
00:00:46.164 --> 00:00:48.860
so retirement is scheduled, not forgotten.
